	"department": "MUSIC",
	"description": [
		"Students explore the intersections of music and community engagement through case studies on topics such as music and healthcare, education, Indigenous cultural agency, development, and immigration. Coursework includes a significant project developing a partnership between students and local community organizations. Students build skills in reading, writing, oral communication, project management, and community relations. Assignments include reading, listening, written reflections, research on issues relevant to community partners, and on- and off-campus engagement with community partners. Offered alternate years in spring semester. Prerequisite: MUSIC 141 Introduction to Musicology and MUSIC 237 Local and Global Musicking."
